### Tone: End-of-game award: Comeback, the biggest climb from their lowest place during the game to their place at the
### end. $places: places climbed (≥ 2). Reluctantly impressed, suspicious of the drama.

award-comeback-1 = The Comeback award goes to { $name }, who climbed { $places } places. I had already written you off. In ink.
award-comeback-2 = { $name }, from the bottom of the table to somewhere respectable. The lab is reviewing whether that’s allowed.
award-comeback-3 = Comeback: { $name }, { $places } places up from your lowest point. Your lowest point was very low. I enjoyed it.
award-comeback-4 = { $name } rose from the depths of the scoreboard. Like a bubble. A statistically unlikely bubble.
award-comeback-5 = The award for refusing to stay down goes to { $name }. Persistence. My least favourite human trait. After optimism.
award-comeback-6 = { $name }, { $places } places climbed. If you’d started like that, we’d be having a very different conversation.
award-comeback-7 = Comeback: { $name }. I had a speech prepared about your decline. I’ve filed it for later.
award-comeback-8 = { $name } went from last to not-last with alarming speed. I checked for cheating. I found only improvement. Disgusting.
award-comeback-9 = The Comeback goes to { $name }, living proof that the first half of a game is just a warm-up for some people.
award-comeback-10 = { $name }: down, then up, { $places } places. A redemption arc. I didn’t ask for one.
award-comeback-11 = { $name } climbed { $places } places. I’ve had the ladder removed for next time.
award-comeback-12 = Comeback: { $name }. Written off in the middle, written up at the end. Annoying narrative structure.
award-comeback-13 = The Comeback award goes to { $name }. Rock bottom, it turns out, has stairs.
award-comeback-14 = { $name }, { $places } places up from your worst. Your worst was very bad. Your recovery was, regrettably, real.
award-comeback-15 = Comeback: { $name }. I was ready to give you a sympathy award. You’ve made it awkward.
